cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite the repository and the mathematical sources recorded in formalization.yaml."
type: software
title: "Robin1984: a Lean formalization of Robin's 1984 criterion for the Riemann hypothesis"
authors:
  - family-names: "Whidden"
    given-names: "Jonas"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 formalization of Guy Robin's equivalence between the Riemann
  hypothesis and the strict divisor-sum inequality above 5040, including the
  reduction to colossally abundant integers, the Nicolas--Landau converse
  argument, and exact finite certificates.
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/kimihiro64/Robin1984"
url: "https://github.com/kimihiro64/Robin1984"
keywords:
  - "Lean 4"
  - "formalized mathematics"
  - "Riemann hypothesis"
  - "Robin's inequality"
  - "colossally abundant numbers"
  - "number theory"
